    {"id": "54296b92-91d3-4d44-9575-27f4a736966d", "term": "sensitivity (dB SPL/mW) / Loudspeaker sensitivity (dB SPL/1W/1m)", "verdict": "MINOR", "suggestions": [{"field": "definition", "severity": "Low", "issue": "The term title names two senses - 'sensitivity (dB SPL/mW)' and 'Loudspeaker sensitivity (dB SPL/1W/1m)' - but the definition and the rest of the entry cover only the loudspeaker (dB SPL per 1 W at 1 m) sense. The dB SPL/mW sense (headphone/earphone/in-ear sensitivity, stated as SPL for a 1 mW drive) is never defined, leaving half the disambiguated title unaddressed.", "suggestion": "Add a short clause covering the dB SPL/mW sense, e.g., 'For headphones and in-ear monitors, sensitivity is instead stated as SPL produced for 1 mW of input (dB SPL/mW), reflecting how loud they play for a given drive level - distinct from the loudspeaker dB SPL/1W/1m figure.'"}]},
